Text:
1. Tribe Trial features a different powerful Boss each day. All members can challenge the Boss with unlimited attempts;

2. Challenging the Boss will be rewarded with Tribe Coin, Hero EXP, Hero Fragment and so on; 

3. When the Boss' HP is reduced to certain amounts, the Boss will be enhanced;

4. The total amount of DMG dealt by all Tribe members to the Boss will be ranked with other Tribes for rewards;

5. First challenge every day is rewarded with 30 Tribe Badges.

1. A Tribe can have a maximum of 15 members at the beginning. This limit can be increased to a maximum of 30 by leveling up the Tribe;

2. A Tribe has a Chief, Elders and ordinary members. An Elder has the power to approve applications and expel members. A Chief has all the powers of an Elder and the right to disband the Tribe. A Chief can't quit their Tribe;

3. All Tribe members can earn Tribe Contribution Badges by participating in Tribe events. The Badge can be used to level up the Tribe. The number of members earning the Badge every day cannot exceed the current maximum number of members in the Tribe;

4. Certain Tribe features are only unlocked when the Tribe reaches the required levels;

5. All members can send chest help requests, which allow other members to provide help for free. When the amount of help received reaches a certain level, a reward chest will be unlocked.

1. Tribe Trial features a different powerful Boss each day with different super abilities;

2. All members can challenge the Boss with unlimited attempts, but the rewards of each tier can only be claimed once;

3. All members can earn 30 Tribe Contribution Badges for the first challenge every day. The number of members earning the Badge every day cannot exceed the current maximum number of members in the Tribe;

4. The Boss cannot be defeated. When losing certain HP, it will be enhanced. To deal as much DMG as possible, the challenger must wisely deploy Heroes according to the Boss' weakness;

5. Tribe Coin, obtained through challenging the Boss, can be used to redeem items in Tribe Store;

6. The total amount of DMG dealt by all Tribe members to the Boss will be ranked with other Tribes for rewards!

7. After joining a Cross-Server Tribe, your tribe will compete against tribes from the tribe’s server.

1. Storm Battlefield has 10 Battle Zones where players compete individually. The event starts at 10:00 every Monday and ends at 23:00 every Saturday;

2. Storm Battlefield has 5 ranks that are Bronze, Silver, Gold, Glory, and King. Each rank has 5 sub-ranks except King;

3. Each win earns a Victory Star. A rank promotion happens when a player wins another challenge with 3 Victory Stars. Losing a challenge costs 1 Star in Gold and Glory ranks and can cause rank demotion;

4. Each challenge costs 1 Storm Battlefield Ticket. Every 2 hours generates 1 free Ticket. Players can buy the Ticket with Diamond or watch videos to gain more;

5. Players will be matched with rivals of similar ranks. The challenged player loses nothing when they are defeated;

6. Reaching a certain rank for the first time each week will result in a rank reward. At the end of the event, players will receive mails containing the rewards based on their final rank.
